Event loop tests
================

Behaviour tests for QEventLoop: timers, posted events, socket notifiers,
nested loops, cross-thread wake-ups, X11 event handling and the
coexistence with GLib sources (GDBus, g_idle_add, g_main_loop_run).
They were written to compare the stock select() loop with a GLib based
loop and are not part of the normal build ("make" does not touch this
directory; there is no .pro file on purpose).

Build against the library of this source tree (configure + make first):

    tests/eventloop/build.sh            # binaries in tests/eventloop/build
    tests/eventloop/build.sh -asan      # with -fsanitize=address,undefined

Run:

    tests/eventloop/build/looptest      # non-GUI checks
    tests/eventloop/build/looptest gui  # also X11 checks (needs $DISPLAY)
    tests/eventloop/build/t2            # GLib main context after ~QApplication

looptest prints one PASS/FAIL line per check and exits with the number
of failures (0 = all passed). The stock select() loop does not dispatch
GLib sources at all, so the GLib/GDBus checks fail there by design.

Needs: g++, pkg-config, GLib/GIO development files (gio-2.0), libX11,
and a D-Bus session bus for the GDBus checks.
